WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.023
(somber music)

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.680
- [Jacqueline] When I lived in Queens,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.903
I went to the beauty
parlor every two weeks;

00:00:11.748 --> 00:00:16.748
I still do it here in this
independent living community.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.563
It's the same routine.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.440
This routine is my life;

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.353
I have been used to it ever
since I came to America.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:32.450
Look, I'm 91 years old, and I
can't stop the aging process

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.663
but I try to remedy whatever I can.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.150
- [Thelma] If you want to
call it a beauty routine,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.740
see, I don't; I call it just
taking care of yourself.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.983
I do it as part of my living.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.510
I don't think I feel beautiful,

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.703
I feel like I'm Thelma.

00:00:52.703 --> 00:00:56.370
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:01:07.014 --> 00:01:09.931
(soft piano music)

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.383
- [René] Change is hard.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.310
Change is hard at any age.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.900
But being a senior and leaving your home

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.370
and leaving familiar
faces and starting new;

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.743
routine's important.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.220
So if they're in the habit

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.750
of getting their hair done
on a Friday at one o'clock,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.773
they still want Friday at one o'clock.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.030
I'm René Carpenito. I'm
the salon coordinator

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.563
and hair stylist at Riverwalk salon.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.640
I've been here for fourteen years,

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.600
and working in a residence like this,

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.930
it does give you
enjoyment, being with them,

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.190
it makes them feel good

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.640
because that's what they're
supposed to be doing.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.510
They've been through it all.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.250
Doing their hair and making them pretty

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.640
and making them feel good,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.253
you also help them get through
their day a little easier.

00:02:05.521 --> 00:02:08.688
(somber violin music)

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.350
- [Jacqueline] I was born in 1927.

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:18.110
I was a teenager during
the holocaust in France.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.580
There were days when
you couldn't take a bath

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.860
because there was nothing,

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.740
but during the war I had one lipstick,

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.920
and I remember it was called Rouge Baiser,

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:32.113
which means red kiss.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:39.800
Lipstick made me feel beautiful,
so it's important to me

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.036
to keep myself clean and to keep myself

00:02:43.036 --> 00:02:45.193
looking the best I can.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:52.430
We came to this country
after the war in 1947.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.660
I met my husband.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.963
I was married 65 years.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.250
After my husband died I felt very lonely,

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.730
and I was in terrible
shape when I came here;

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:08.444
but the beauty salon is
downstairs on the lower floor.

00:03:08.444 --> 00:03:09.350
Morning.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.820
I go to the beauty parlor every two weeks.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.930
It's an intimate place.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:16.580
I talk to people.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.370
You feel very good going there;

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.423
I know that I'll come
out and I'll look decent.

00:03:25.612 --> 00:03:29.210
(gentle piano music)

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:33.470
- [Thelma] Two years ago
my husband fell, and died.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.293
I never thought that
this would happen to me.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.770
At the beginning I froze;

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.203
and I said, "Who am I?"

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.650
Always dressed, see?

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:47.423
This is the way my family
was; we always dressed.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:55.443
This is my life today,
it cannot be what it was.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:01.480
I have to maintain who I am.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.660
I love clothes.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.230
My hair is the same as
it was when I was twenty,

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:11.680
It's very simple and I
don't want to lose myself;

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.283
so far, I have not.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.423
- [René] Thelma's been here

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.250
a little while.
Good morning.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:23.410
- [René] She's very sharp;
she's very into fashion.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.430
Thelma has her style;
she knows what she likes.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.757
- [Thelma] And not too short down here.

00:04:28.757 --> 00:04:31.760
- [René] And I do what she
likes, week after week.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.830
She shares a lot of stories
and she goes out often,

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.652
and she's just living
life and enjoying life.

00:04:38.652 --> 00:04:41.910
(gentle piano music)

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.690
I feel like coming here
gives me the opportunity

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.423
to have 95 grandmothers.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.810
It's a very comfortable place to be.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:50.760
They're getting older,

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.520
and their life is getting a little harder,

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.850
so when you're the one that
makes their day better,

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.850
that gives you so much more fulfillment.

00:04:58.962 --> 00:05:02.045
(gentle piano music)

